.TH PMAT 1 "August 2024" "2.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmat \- Pragmatic AI MCP Agent Toolkit for code quality and AI context generation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmat
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
PMAT (Pragmatic AI MCP Agent Toolkit) is a zero-configuration AI context generation and code quality toolkit with Claude Code Agent Mode integration.

It provides comprehensive code analysis, quality enforcement following Toyota Way standards, and continuous monitoring capabilities through MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B context
Generate AI-optimized context for the current codebase
.TP
.B quality-gate
Run quality checks with configurable thresholds
.TP
.B analyze
Perform various code analysis operations (complexity, SATD, dead code)
.TP  
.B agent
Claude Code Agent Mode operations (start, stop, status, mcp-server)
.TP
.B refactor
AI-assisted refactoring suggestions and automation

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version information and exit
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug mode with detailed logging

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate AI context for current directory:
.B pmat context

.TP
Run quality gates with strict enforcement:
.B pmat quality-gate --strict

.TP  
Start Claude Code Agent Mode:
.B pmat agent mcp-server

.TP
Analyze code complexity:
.B pmat analyze complexity --top-files 10

.TP
Start continuous monitoring service:
.B pmat agent start --config /etc/pmat/agent-production.toml

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are located in /etc/pmat/:
.TP
.I agent-development.toml
Development environment settings
.TP  
.I agent-production.toml
Production deployment configuration
.TP
.I agent-ci.toml
CI/CD pipeline integration settings

.SH CLAUDE CODE INTEGRATION
To integrate with Claude Code, add the following to your settings.json:

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pmat": {
      "command": "pmat", 
      "args": ["agent", "mcp-server"],
      "env": {}
    }
  }
}

.SH SERVICE MODE
PMAT can run as a systemd service for continuous monitoring:

sudo systemctl enable pmat-agent
sudo systemctl start pmat-agent

Service logs: /var/log/pmat-agent/
Service state: /var/lib/pmat-agent/

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
.TP
.B 2  
Quality gate failure (code quality below thresholds)
.TP
.B 3
Configuration error
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by user (Ctrl+C)

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pmat/
System configuration directory
.TP
.I /var/lib/pmat-agent/
Service state and data directory  
.TP
.I /var/log/pmat-agent/
Service log directory
.TP
.I ~/.config/pmat/
User configuration directory

